status.comment:
Built in e1fc9b7e, 0cc66b41, 3741a2ad and bfb0bba7.

Flow: without write access, dragging out of an idea into empty space opens 'Propose a space'. The choices are:
- a new space from its central aim (the title names the space and becomes its one idea, intrinsic value 1);
- one of your spaces;
- one on another server by its address.
The pitch becomes the hypothesis. The offer is stored as a guest note with the drop position (relativePosition).

Visibility (notes.offers): the proposer and the space's writers see the offer in the graph; nobody else does. It is drawn as an unconfirmed supporter: label '· offered', dotted outline, no value flowing. The proposer's own offers open in place. A card beside the offered space shows Accept or Decline to writers and Withdraw to the proposer. Accepting keeps the position.

Editing in place: a space on this server that the viewer may write opens editable. Its ideas join the store, and utils/idea-spaces.ts routes each request to the idea's space; cross-space connections are refused.

Verified: backend tests in guest/notes.test.ts; frontend tests data-repo-nodes.spec and idea-spaces.test. A probe server with a browser covered guest offer → owner accept, and dragging out of the central idea created an idea inside the offered space.

Open:
- a space on another server opens read-only (needs 1f6f2c46);
- ideas of a pending space show 0 as their value total in the side panel;
- undo does not cover edits made in a space opened in place.
